# Invariant 8: an application message is accepted only from a device whose leaf is in the current
# tree (403 E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT), and only when its authenticated_data - the franking commitment C -
# is exactly 32 bytes (422 E_COMMITMENT_INVALID). Bob's commitments of 31, 33 and 0 bytes are
# refused while his well-formed message goes through; once the instance's Remove of bob is
# committed, his next message is refused because his leaf is gone, and the group carries on.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8f8 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
sync carol
expect_reject E_COMMITMENT_INVALID send_bad_commitment bob chat 31
expect_reject E_COMMITMENT_INVALID send_bad_commitment bob chat 33
expect_reject E_COMMITMENT_INVALID send_bad_commitment bob chat 0
send bob chat a 32-byte commitment is accepted
expect_decrypts carol chat a 32-byte commitment is accepted
kick alice bob
commit alice
sync carol
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT send bob chat my leaf is gone
send carol chat the group carries on
expect_decrypts alice chat the group carries on
